{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-223708",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-y & =0 \\\\ y(y-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\ny=0\\,\\text{or}\\,y-1=0,\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\ny=0\\,\\text{or}\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=0$ and $y=1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
